  "productionFlowReviewed": [
    "Original GSON marker is authoritative; same legacy loginUi reports precise LOGIN_UI_V2 before authored prelude. No Swift approximation or generic-error fallback is part of backend admission.",
    "BaseSource two methods use original loginUi(state)/loginAction(action,state,form) JSON argument bindings with java===source and null book/chapter. They do not install legacy UI Java or result Map.",
    "Full returned command is parsed/validated before explicit checked login put; rejected/IO/cancel save cannot authorize close/state publication. Original errors/state/login/close protocol order is retained; unknown command keys remain typed transient diagnostics.",
    "Cancellation before/after real checked owner response retains possible/committed effects; no success/close DTO escapes after cancellation. Existing envelope,executor and Service copy effects before post-await checks/cleanup failures.",
    "Both V2 operations join sensitive operation and pre-task fallback sets, so script/Host/parser errors do not expose arbitrary credential-bearing messages. They do not enable legacy login UI callback events.",
    "Same source actor lock/revision,original process,taskID,credential/header/Cookie owners; no Book grant,new store,JSC,fake save or source-route fallback.",
    "App fixture exhaustive switch now explicitly rejects both new operations without default catch-all. Other typed consumers use actual new execution branches or preexisting reject/default/guard forms."
  ],
